# Haryana Schemes, Institutions and Policies

> Two kinds of questions come from this topic: "which scheme was launched
> where and when" and "which university or institute was set up in which
> year". Beti Bachao Beti Padhao began in Panipat, Haryana, which is why
> the state keeps appearing in national-level papers. This lesson lists
> only dated, checkable facts for the schemes and institutions most often
> examined in HSSC CET and Haryana Police papers.

## 1. Welfare and Governance Schemes

| Scheme | What it is | Anchor fact |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Beti Bachao Beti Padhao | National campaign for the girl child, to improve the child sex ratio and promote girls' education | Launched at **Panipat, Haryana, on 22 January 2015** |
| Parivar Pehchan Patra (PPP) | Family-ID database of every family in the state, for delivering benefits and verified data | Launched by Haryana Government in 2015; each family gets an **eight-digit** Family ID linked to birth, death and marriage records |
| Meri Fasal Mera Byora | Online farmer-registration and e-procurement portal for crops | Used for sale at Minimum Support Price; reported in 2022 to cover 14 crops, with farmers registering their crop details |

[definition]
**Parivar Pehchan Patra** is a family database, not a card for one person.
The Family ID is eight digits long and the data is collected with the
family's consent.
[/definition]

Why Haryana for Beti Bachao Beti Padhao? The state had one of the lowest
child sex ratios in India, so the scheme was launched from its soil.
Remember "BBBP = Panipat = 22 January 2015". The common distractors are
Jhajjar, Kurukshetra and Sonipat, or a launch date of 2014.

Meri Fasal Mera
Byora is about **crops and farmers**; Parivar Pehchan Patra is about
**families**. Mixing the two is the usual trap.

## 2. Haryana Day and the Basics

**Haryana Day** is observed on **1 November**, the day in 1966 when Haryana
was carved out of Punjab as the 17th state. Exams ask the date (1 November) and the year (1966).

| Item | Fact |
| --- | --- |
| Formation | 1 November 1966 |
| First CM | Bhagwat Dayal Sharma |
| Capital | Chandigarh (shared with Punjab) |

## 3. Universities

| University | Place | Established |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Kurukshetra University | Kurukshetra | 11 January 1956 (on the bank of Brahma Sarovar; NAAC A++ in 2024) |
| Maharshi Dayanand University (MDU) | Rohtak | 1976 (Act passed 1975); first called Rohtak University, renamed in 1977 |
| Chaudhary Charan Singh Haryana Agricultural University (CCS HAU) | Hisar | 2 February 1970 as Haryana Agricultural University; renamed after Charan Singh on 31 October 1991 |
| Chaudhary Devi Lal University (CDLU) | Sirsa | 2 April 2003 |

Memory trick: the oldest university in the list is **Kurukshetra (1956)**,
then HAU (1970), MDU (1976) and finally CDLU (2003). The two agricultural
and general names are easy to swap: **Hisar = agriculture, Rohtak = MDU,
Sirsa = Devi Lal**.

## 4. National Institutes

| Institution | Place | Facts |
| --- | --- | --- |
| NIT Kurukshetra | Kurukshetra | Founded in 1963 as Regional Engineering College; renamed NIT in 2002 |
| IIM Rohtak | Rohtak (Sunaria, NH-10) | Foundation stone 16 November 2009; classes began June 2010; an Institute of National Importance |
| AIIMS Rewari | Majra Bhalkhi village, Rewari | Foundation stone laid by the Prime Minister on 16 February 2024; planned about 720-bed hospital plus a 30-bed AYUSH block; under the Pradhan Mantri Swasthya Suraksha Yojana (PMSSY) |

[example]
A question asks: "Which Haryana institute had its foundation stone
laid in February 2024?" The answer is AIIMS Rewari, not IIM Rohtak. The IIM
dates to 2009-10. Check the year in the question: 2009 or 2010 points to
IIM, 2024 points to AIIMS. AIIMS Rewari was at foundation stage in 2024,
so do not claim a full-service opening unless the question gives a later
date.
[/example]

## 5. Quick Revision Pairs

- BBBP: Panipat, 22 January 2015.
- PPP: eight-digit family ID, 2015.
- Meri Fasal Mera Byora: crop registration and MSP purchase.
- Kurukshetra University 1956; MDU 1976; CDLU 2003; HAU 1970.
- NIT Kurukshetra: REC 1963, NIT 2002.
- IIM Rohtak: 2010; AIIMS Rewari: stone laid February 2024.

[summary]
Haryana Day: 1 November (1966). BBBP launched at Panipat on 22 January 2015.
Parivar Pehchan Patra: 2015, eight-digit family ID. Meri Fasal Mera Byora:
farmer crop portal for MSP e-procurement. Universities: Kurukshetra 1956,
HAU Hisar 1970 (renamed 1991), MDU Rohtak 1976, CDLU Sirsa 2003. NIT
Kurukshetra: 1963, renamed 2002. IIM Rohtak: 2009 stone, 2010 classes.
AIIMS Rewari: Majra Bhalkhi, foundation stone 16 February 2024.
[/summary]
